      {
        "id": "post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action",
        "kind": "postulate",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Free massive test-particle action",
        "statement": "For a $C^2$ future-directed timelike worldline $x:I\\to M$ on a prescribed smooth, time-oriented Lorentzian background $(M,g,T)$ of signature $(-+++)$, with $m>0$ a fixed primitive mass in kg and $c>0$ in m/s, adopt the stationary-action model\n\n$$S_m[x]=-mc\\int_I\\sqrt{-g(x',x') }\\,d\\lambda.$$\n\nHere λ is an increasing regular parameter, endpoint events are fixed, and admissible variations remain future timelike. The integrand is the proper-time length density, so $S_m=-mc^2\\int d\\tau$; its dimension is action (J s). The adopted premise concerns this ideal free test body only. It is neither a theorem about all matter nor an empirical report, and supplies no backreaction or completeness claim. The flat ideal-clock specialization agrees with [[post-sr-ideal-clocks-and-light]]; adopting this action on a curved background remains a separate premise.\n\nThe cotangent phase-space carrier convention assumes countable choice ACω only; full choice is not assumed.",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-rpm-h-background-and-model-quantities",
          "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
          "post-sr-ideal-clocks-and-light"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "post-sr-ideal-clocks-and-light": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-rpm-h-background-and-model-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space": "formulation-prerequisite"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Andrew Hanson, Tullio Regge and Claudio Teitelboim, Constrained Hamiltonian Systems, Part 1, complete monograph",
              "url": "https://scholarworks.iu.edu/dspace/bitstreams/0e1d11ee-2741-4da4-83ed-b7cabc0cd7d6/download",
              "locator": "Complete 35-page Part 1; Chapter II, printed pp. 27–30, relativistic spinless point particle."
            },
            {
              "title": "B. F. Chagas-Filho, Free massless particles and extended space-time algebra, comparison for the distinct massive square-root action",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0401091",
              "locator": "§1, pp. 1–2."
            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 2,
        "physical_scope": "Classical spinless structureless point test body with fixed primitive mass m>0 on a prescribed background; excludes self-field, radiation reaction, finite size, spin and quantum effects.",
        "library": "physics"
      },
      {
        "id": "post-rpm-h-massless-shell-action",
        "kind": "postulate",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Separate massless shell action",
        "statement": "On a prescribed background $(M,g,T)$, adopt a distinct massless classical particle model with fields $x:I\\to M$, $p(\\lambda)\\in T^*_{x(\\lambda)}M$, and a positive smooth multiplier $e(\\lambda)>0$:\n\n$$S_0[x,p,e]=\\int_I\\left[p_a x'^a-eC_0(x,p)\\right]d\\lambda,\\qquad C_0=\\tfrac12g^{ab}p_ap_b.$$\n\nVariations of $p,e$ are independent; the physical branch is $p\\ne0$, $p^\\sharp$ future null. With all spacetime coordinates measured in metres and dimensionless λ, $p_a$ has units kg m/s, $C_0$ has units kg²m²/s² and $e$ has units s/kg, making the action J s. Other parameter units scale $e$ accordingly. This is a separate adopted model: null curves have no proper-time parameter, the model does not arise by setting $m=0$ in $P=mU$, and its positive momentum scale is additional initial data. On the nonzero branch, the vertical differential is $d_pC_0=p^\\sharp\\ne0$: nondegeneracy of $g^{-1}$ and $p\\ne0$ give $p^\\sharp\\ne0$. Hence the shell is a regular primary constraint in the sense of [[def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system]]. This postulate is not an empirical observation or a deduction from the massive model.\n\nThe cotangent phase-space carrier convention assumes countable choice ACω only; full choice is not assumed.",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-rpm-h-background-and-model-quantities",
          "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
          "def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-rpm-h-background-and-model-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space": "formulation-prerequisite"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "W. F. Chagas-Filho, Free massless particles and extended space-time algebra, complete paper",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0401091",
              "locator": "§§1–2, pp. 1–3, einbein action and massless constraint."
            },
            {
              "title": "Sean M. Carroll, Lecture Notes on General Relativity, complete lecture notes (arXiv:gr-qc/9712019v1)",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/gr-qc/9712019",
              "locator": "Complete 238-page notes; Chapter 1, printed pp. 25–27, and Chapter 3, printed pp. 68–72; full relevant sections inspected."
            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 2,
        "physical_scope": "Separate classical massless test-particle formulation with nonzero future-null momentum; no proper-time parameter, no mU identification and no empirical realization claim.",
        "library": "physics"
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-rpm-h-constraint-consistency",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Constraint consistency for a regular first-order model",
        "statement": "Let $I\\subset\\mathbb R$ be an open interval and $(P,\\omega)$ a symplectic manifold. Let $\\chi_a:I\\times P\\to\\mathbb R$ be smooth and suppose the covectors $d_z\\chi_a(\\lambda,z)$ are linearly independent at every $z\\in N_\\lambda:=\\{z:\\chi_1(\\lambda,z)=\\cdots=\\chi_r(\\lambda,z)=0\\}$; this is the regular constraint condition of [[def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system]] on each slice. Let $H_c:I\\times P\\to\\mathbb R$ be a smooth ambient extension of a specified descended Hamiltonian. Work in a Darboux chart with coordinates $(q^i,p_i)$ and local potential $\\theta=p_i\\,dq^i$, so $d\\theta=-\\omega$ under the convention $\\omega=dq^i\\wedge dp_i$; paths stay in this chart.\nFor any compact interval $[a,b]\\subset I$ with $a<b$, paths $z:[a,b]\\to P$ that stay in the chart and smooth multipliers $u^a:[a,b]\\to\\mathbb R$ have action\n\n$$I[z,u]=\\int_a^b\\left[\\theta(\\dot z)-H_c(\\lambda,z)-u^a(\\lambda)\\chi_a(\\lambda,z)\\right]d\\lambda.$$\n\nFixed-endpoint variations of $z$ and unrestricted variations of $u$ imply $z(\\lambda)\\in N_\\lambda$ and $\\dot z=X_{H_c(\\lambda,\\cdot)}+u^a(\\lambda)X_{\\chi_a(\\lambda,\\cdot)}$. A trajectory remains in the moving level set only when\n\n$$\\partial_\\lambda\\chi_a+\\{\\chi_a,H_c(\\lambda,\\cdot)\\}+u^b(\\lambda)\\{\\chi_a,\\chi_b\\}=0\\quad\\text{on }N_\\lambda.$$\n\nFor constraints independent of $\\lambda$, the first term is zero.",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
          "def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system",
          "thm-rpm-h-canonical-poisson-and-flow",
          "thm-darboux-theorem",
          "thm-cm-stationarity-iff-euler-lagrange"
        ],
