      {
        "id": "thm-rpm-h-homogeneous-massive-shell",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Massive square-root Legendre map and its future shell",
        "statement": "Let $(M,g,T)$ be a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold, $m,c>0$, and $L(x,V)=-mc\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}$ on the future timelike tangent cone. Its fibre derivative is\n\n$$p_a=mc\\frac{g_{ab}V^b}{s},\\qquad s=\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}>0.$$\n\nThe velocity Hessian is $mc(g_{ab}/s+V_aV_b/s^3)$, has kernel exactly $\\mathbb RV$, and rank three. The image consists exactly of the future shell $\\Sigma_m^+=\\{(x,p)\\in T^*M:g_x^{-1}(p,p)=-m^2c^2,\\ p^\\sharp\\text{ future}\\}$. Each fibre is a connected positive ray, and the Legendre map is a surjective submersion onto this embedded image. Its energy $p(V)-L$ is zero; the map has no local inverse in the four-velocity direction.",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects",
          "def-rpm-spacetime-observer-and-worldline",
          "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
