      {
        "id": "thm-rpm-h-regular-local-gauge-slice",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "A transverse local gauge condition gives a second-class slice",
        "statement": "Let $\\chi_1,\\ldots,\\chi_r$ be regular first-class constraints on $N$ as in [[thm-rpm-h-first-class-local-reduction]]. Let $\\phi_1,\\ldots,\\phi_r$ be smooth gauge functions such that $A_{ab}=\\{\\chi_a,\\phi_b\\}$ is invertible on their common zero set near a point. Then the combined constraint matrix for $(\\chi,\\phi)$ is invertible there, so the combined surface is second class and carries the Dirac symplectic form. After shrinking the neighborhood, each nearby characteristic leaf intersects the gauge surface in exactly one point within that coordinate neighborhood. This is a local slice assertion only. When $r=0$ the characteristic leaves are points and the empty gauge condition is immediate; the proof below treats $r\\ge1$.",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system",
          "thm-rpm-h-first-class-local-reduction",
          "thm-rpm-h-second-class-dirac-bracket",
