      {
        "id": "thm-rpm-h-first-order-action-and-geodesics",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "First-order shell action yields massive and null geodesics",
        "statement": "Let $(M,g,T)$ be a prescribed smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold with signature $(-+++)$. Work in a spacetime chart on a compact parameter interval $[a,b]$ with $a<b$; take $x,p,e$ smooth on a neighbourhood of that interval, $e>0$, $m\\ge0$, and $c>0$. Select stationary triples on the future shell branch after taking the independent variations: when $m>0$, $p^\\sharp$ is future timelike; when $m=0$, require $p\\ne0$ and $p^\\sharp$ future null. Set $C_m=\\tfrac12(g^{ab}p_ap_b+m^2c^2)$ and define the first-order functional\n\n$$I_m[x,p,e]=\\int_a^b\\left(p_ax'^a-eC_m(x,p)\\right)d\\lambda.$$\n\nTake independent smooth variations of $p,e$ and fixed-endpoint variations of $x$. Stationarity on the chart segment is equivalent to\n\n$$x'^a=e g^{ab}p_b,\\quad p'_a=-\\tfrac e2\\partial_a g^{bc}p_bp_c,\\quad C_m=0.$$\n\nOn the massive future branch $m>0$, these equations are equivalent to stationary paths of the mathematical square-root functional $S[x]=-mc\\int_a^b\\sqrt{-g(x\\prime,x\\prime)}\\,d\\lambda$ on future-timelike curves with fixed endpoints; the fibre-derivative covector is $p=mc\\,x'^\\flat/\\sqrt{-g(x',x')}$, and proper-time gauge has $e=1/m$. For the separate nonzero future-null branch $m=0$, the equations describe a null geodesic with an arbitrary positive parameter multiplier; no proper-time parameter exists. In both cases the unparameterized path is a geodesic, and no existence or completeness claim is made.",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects",
          "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
          "thm-gr-nondegenerate-levi-civita-and-tensor-derivative",
          "def-geodesic-of-an-affine-connection",
