      {
        "id": "thm-rpm-h-inertial-time-reduced-hamiltonian",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Free shell in inertial time has the square-root Hamiltonian",
        "statement": "In affine Minkowski space with $x^0=ct$, let $m\\ge0$, $p_i$ be spatial momentum components and $p_i\\ne0$ for $m=0$. On the future shell, $p_0=-E/c$, where\n\n$$E(\\mathbf p)=\\sqrt{m^2c^4+c^2|\\mathbf p|^2}.$$\n\nOn any compact interval $J=[t_1,t_2]$ of inertial time, the gauge $x^0=ct$ reduces the first-order shell action to\n\n$$I_J=\\int_{t_1}^{t_2}\\left(p_i\\dot q^i-E(\\mathbf p)\\right)dt,\\qquad q^i=x^i.$$\n\nThe gauge pair $C_m=0$, $\\psi=x^0-ct=0$ is second class because $\\{C_m,\\psi\\}=-P^0\\ne0$ on the future shell; its Dirac reduction gives the canonical spatial bracket. The reduced Hamilton equations are $\\dot q^i=c^2p_i/E$, $\\dot p_i=0$, agreeing with the unreduced characteristic trajectories. On this full flat future shell every characteristic line meets each inertial-time slice once; this global assertion does not extend by this proof to a curved temporal chart.",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
          "def-sr-affine-minkowski-model",
          "thm-rpm-h-flat-shell-global-reduction",
          "thm-rpm-h-first-order-action-and-geodesics",
          "thm-rpm-h-second-class-dirac-bracket",
          "thm-rpm-h-canonical-poisson-and-flow"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "thm-rpm-h-canonical-poisson-and-flow": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-rpm-h-second-class-dirac-bracket": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-sr-affine-minkowski-model": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-rpm-h-flat-shell-global-reduction": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-rpm-h-first-order-action-and-geodesics": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Sean M. Carroll, Lecture Notes on General Relativity, complete lecture notes (arXiv:gr-qc/9712019v1)",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/gr-qc/9712019",
              "locator": "Complete 238-page notes; Chapter 1, printed pp. 25–27, and Chapter 3, printed pp. 68–72; full relevant sections inspected."
            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 5,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "physical_scope": "Flat free particle on the full future shell; inertial time gauge is global here only because P0 is strictly positive.",
        "library": "physics"
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-rpm-h-action-mechanical-momentum",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Square-root action momentum equals massive mechanical momentum",
        "statement": "For the massive square-root Lagrangian $L=-mc\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}$ on a prescribed smooth Lorentzian background, its fibre derivative is $p=mc\\,V^\\flat/\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}$. If τ is proper time along the timelike curve, $U=dx/d\\tau=cV/\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}$, so the raised momentum is $p^\\sharp=mU$. In flat spacetime this agrees with the adopted special-relativistic mechanical momentum convention. This is a model identity, not a measurement.",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-rpm-h-background-and-model-quantities",
          "thm-rpm-h-homogeneous-massive-shell",
          "thm-sr-proper-time-and-observer-decomposition",
          "post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action",
