      {
        "id": "pthm-rpm-h-massive-and-null-time-motion",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Massive and null free particles in inertial time",
        "statement": "In the flat inertial-time model of [[thm-rpm-h-inertial-time-reduced-hamiltonian]], the coordinate velocity is $\\dot{\\mathbf q}=c^2\\mathbf p/E$. For $m>0$, its Euclidean magnitude is strictly less than $c$; for the separate massless model $m=0$ with $\\mathbf p\\ne0$, its magnitude is exactly $c$. Spatial momentum is constant in both cases. These are deductions from the adopted free actions, not experimental measurements.",
        "deps": [
