      {
        "id": "thm-rpm-h-temporal-shell-reduction",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "A curved temporal chart gives a local reduced Hamiltonian",
        "statement": "Let $m\\ge0$ and $c>0$. Assume a temporal product chart with lapse-shift data $(N,\\beta,h)$ as in [[def-rpm-h-temporal-chart-data]], all four coordinates measured in metres. On the future shell $C_m=\\tfrac12(g^{ab}p_ap_b+m^2c^2)=0$, define\n\n$$\\kappa=\\sqrt{m^2c^2+h^{ij}p_ip_j},\\quad p_0=\\beta^ip_i-N\\kappa,\\quad H(t,q,p)=-cp_0=c(N\\kappa-\\beta^ip_i).$$\n\nFor $m=0$, require $p_i\\ne0$. On any compact interval $J=[t_1,t_2]$ whose path stays in the chart, the gauge $x^0=ct$ reduces the first-order action to $\\int_{t_1}^{t_2}(p_i\\dot q^i-H)dt$, and its variational equations on the interior of $J$ are exactly $\\dot q^i=H_{p_i}$, $\\dot p_i=-H_{q^i}$. The construction is local to this chart and intervals transverse to its time slices; no global curved-space gauge or quotient is asserted.",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-rpm-h-temporal-chart-data",
          "def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects",
          "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
          "thm-rpm-h-first-order-action-and-geodesics",
          "thm-rpm-h-canonical-poisson-and-flow",
          "thm-a-regular-level-set-is-an-embedded-submanifold",
          "lem-gr-observer-pairing-with-future-causal-vectors"
        ],
